        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-12T15:19:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not familiar with the SkRuntimeShaderBuilder API. Are there other constructors that make passing in the builder over just the sk_sp\u003cSkRuntimeEffect\u003e significant?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "ef81f371502996f37fbe15cdd5101884293a0660",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f0acfbb_6149d8e8",
        "filename": "gm/runtimeimagefilter.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-12T15:34:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The builder owns an SkData with the uniforms, and an array of child shaders. The main thing it\u0027s doing here is serving as a way to retain all of that other state (while still letting us dynamically bind to the \"input\" child). That lets you make a runtime shader that has an image-shader child (lookup table, whatever, hanging off the side), and still use that in the image filter DAG.",
      "parentUuid": "8b85f9be_b875676d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "ef81f371502996f37fbe15cdd5101884293a0660",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "960f222c_3e426acd",
        "filename": "gm/runtimeimagefilter.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-13T00:51:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, so the old hidden factory only supported a runtime shader that had one child, and that was always late bound to the IF input.",
      "parentUuid": "9f0acfbb_6149d8e8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "ef81f371502996f37fbe15cdd5101884293a0660",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c31e368_28f03392",
        "filename": "include/effects/SkImageFilters.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-12T15:19:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"If null the builder can have up to one child shader, which automatically binds the input param. If the builder has no child shaders, the input param is ignored.\"\n?\n\nI\u0027d like to keep the \"automatically\" in the docs, but I\u0027m flexible on how we handle runtime effects with 0 children. Realistically, those cases could just go to SkImageFilters::Shader() with an SkShader created from the runtime effect instead.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 347,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "ef81f371502996f37fbe15cdd5101884293a0660",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c9be2b3_959cf235",
        "filename": "include/effects/SkImageFilters.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 5020
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-18T16:45:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll update the docs regarding automatically.\n\nFor the other doc update we have two choices if the builder has no shaders.\n\n1) return null\n2) internally turn this into SkImageFilters::Shader() on the callers behalf\n\nMichael, given that you know more about this API than I do I will defer to you on which behavior we go with.",
      "parentUuid": "3c31e368_28f03392",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 347,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "ef81f371502996f37fbe15cdd5101884293a0660",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49a79e20_eec55392",
        "filename": "include/effects/SkImageFilters.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T17:43:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think returning null is appropriate, given the new language in the API doc, which I like.\n\nI am good landing this as-is, but wdyt think about tweaking the public name? The only reason I ask is to differentiate it from the 0-input ::Shader() factory. Except that we don\u0027t yet support bounds inset/outsetting, this really is a runtime image filter, so could we go with SkImageFilters::Runtime() or RuntimeFilter()? Or is it better to stick with RuntimeShader() since you\u0027re passing in a runtimeshaderbuilder?\n\nMy thinking was that as we expand the capabilities of runtime image filters to allow for bounds specification somehow, they would share the same factory name as this one, but with more args.",
      "parentUuid": "1c9be2b3_959cf235",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 347,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "ef81f371502996f37fbe15cdd5101884293a0660",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
